OL,3,CProgramme listings for THU 30 APR
OL,4,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,5,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,6,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,7,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,8,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,9,     Geverything in between.
OL,10,G2330F'Round Midnight
OL,11,     GSoweto presents another hour of
OL,12,     Gbest in jazz, with a focus on
OL,13,     GInternational Jazz Day and this
OL,14,     Gyear's host city of Chicago.
OL,15,G0030FThrough the Night
OL,16,     GGeorgian pianist Elisabeth
OL,17,     GLeonskaja performs Schubert's
OL,18,     GFour Impromptus D.899; joined by
OL,19,     GBudapest-born pianist Mihaly
OL,20,     GBerecz to play a selection of
OL,21,     GBrahms's Hungarian Dances.
